## Existing Conflict-Related Code

**None implemented on the server.** Only stubs and infrastructure:

| Location | Status |
|----------|--------|
| `slots.service.ts` | Returns `conflicts: []`; no 409 on add/update |
| `global-exception.filter.ts` | Ready to pass 409 body as raw JSON array |
| `slots.controller.ts` | Swagger docs describe 409 responses |
| `client/src/api.ts` | `ConflictError` handles 409 from API |
| `client/src/components/SlotModal.tsx` | Displays conflict list on 409 |

**409 pattern expected by tests:** throw `HttpException` with status 409 and body = array of conflicting `SlotDto` objects (no wrapper):

```typescript
throw new HttpException(conflictingSlots, HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
```

The global filter passes that array through directly:

```21:24:/Users/guestaccount/Documents/GitHub/bond-assignment/server/src/filters/global-exception.filter.ts
    if (status === HttpStatus.CONFLICT && exception instanceof HttpException) {
      response.status(status).json(exception.getResponse());
      return;
    }
```

